e internet through its virtual bidding third generation internet auction-style sales technology. It offers services, such as online seller access; salvage estimation; estimating; end-of-life vehicle processing; transportation; vehicle inspection stations; on-demand reporting; title processing and express; loan payoff; flexible vehicle processing programs; buy it now and make an offer; sales process; and dealer services. In addition, the company provides IntelliSeller, an automated tool that leverages its vehicle and sales data to assist its sellers in making vital auction decisions; BluCar to sell vehicles of financial institutions, fleet, and rental car companies; CashForCars.com, CashForCars.ca, CashForCars.de, CashForCars.co.uk, and Cash-for-cars.ie; and national powersport auctions services, which include services through live and online auction platforms to dealers, financial institutions, and original equipment manufacturers. Further, it offers wholesale construction, agriculture, and fleet remarketing services through no-reserve online auctions under Purple Wave brand name; Copart Recycling services; and Copart 360, a technology that captures clear 360-degree views of interiors and exteriors of cars, trucks, and vans. The company sells the vehicles to licensed vehicle dismantlers, rebuilders, repair licenses, used vehicle dealers, and exporters, as well as to the public. Copart, Inc. was incorporated in 1982 and is headquartered in Dallas, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. A. Jayson Adair | Executive Chairman & CEO | Age 56 | Compensation: $351,386 (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 21K people. Revenue per employee of $222K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 12%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $60K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Copart, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $28.8B market cap on $4.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +14% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 9-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $1.3B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 27 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.08\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Management returns a meaningful 5.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 8.6% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 3.2\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 52% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5174289643030863},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $5.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-5482622.25},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 26% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Copart, Inc. (CPRT) Stock Moves -1.91%: What You Should Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3032849/copart-inc-cprt-stock-moves-1-91-what-you-should-know?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_6v3-3032849","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795126501.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (CPRT) Edition","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/24/Trading_the_Move,_Not_the_Narrative:_CPRT_Edition_111826115201_1795063921.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795063921.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Can Copart (NASDAQ:CPRT) Maintain Its Strong Margins Amid Industry Growth?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/industrial/can-copart-nasdaqcprt-maintain-its-strong-margins-amid-industry-growth","date":"2026-11-18","timestamp":1795014240.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"45,000 Copart, Inc. $CPRT Shares Purchased by Ibex Investors LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/16/45000-copart-inc-cprt-shares-purchased-by-ibex-investors-llc.html